---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use — PureFile"
  description="Read PureFile's straightforward terms of use for our free, client-side browser file conversion utilities."
  canonicalUrl="https://purefile.dev/terms"
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <!-- Breadcrumb -->
    <nav class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-surface-500 mb-6" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-brand-600 transition-colors">Home</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="text-surface-900 font-medium" aria-current="page">Terms of Use</span>
    </nav>

    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mb-10 pb-6 border-b border-surface-200">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
        <span class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md text-xs font-semibold bg-surface-100 text-surface-800 border border-surface-200">
          Utility Terms
        </span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-surface-950 tracking-tight">
        Terms of Use
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-surface-500 font-mono">
        Last updated: September 2026
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-sm prose-slate max-w-none space-y-8 text-surface-700 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <!-- Section 1: Acceptance & Service Description -->
      <section class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-surface-200/80 shadow-xs">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-surface-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-md bg-brand-100 text-brand-800 font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center">1</span>
          Description of Service &amp; Acceptance
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          PureFile provides free, client-side browser utilities for formatting, compressing, resizing, and compiling files entirely within your web browser.
        </p>
        <p>
          By accessing or using PureFile, you agree to these Terms of Use. If you do not agree with any part of these terms, you should discontinue using the website.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2: File Ownership & Content -->
      <section class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-surface-200/80 shadow-xs">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-surface-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-md bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center">2</span>
          Your Files &amp; Intellectual Property
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          <strong>You retain 100% ownership and intellectual property rights in all files you process using PureFile.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          Because PureFile executes entirely on your device hardware without uploading your files, we never obtain, store, inspect, claim copyright over, or license any files you process. You are solely responsible for ensuring you have the necessary legal rights to convert and modify the files you choose to process.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3: As-Is Warranty Disclaimer -->
      <section class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-surface-200/80 shadow-xs">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-surface-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-md bg-amber-100 text-amber-800 font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center">3</span>
          "As-Is" Disclaimer &amp; Limitations of Liability
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          PureFile is provided free of charge on an "AS IS" and "AS AVAILABLE" basis, without warranties of any kind, whether express or implied, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or uninterrupted availability.
        </p>
        <p>
          Because file transformations depend on your individual browser capabilities, available RAM, and operating system limits, PureFile and its authors shall not be liable for any data loss, corrupted outputs, browser crashes, or consequential damages resulting from your use of the website. Always maintain original backups of important files before running conversions.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4: Acceptable Use -->
      <section class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-surface-200/80 shadow-xs">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-surface-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-md bg-purple-100 text-purple-800 font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center">4</span>
          Acceptable Use
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          You agree to use PureFile only for lawful purposes. You agree not to attempt to disrupt or compromise the website's static delivery infrastructure or use automated systems to excessively scrape or overwhelm the service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 5: Modifications & Inquiries -->
      <section class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-surface-200/80 shadow-xs">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-surface-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-md bg-surface-200 text-surface-800 font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center">5</span>
          Modifications &amp; Inquiries
        </h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms periodically to reflect changes in our tools or legal requirements. For any inquiries regarding these terms, please visit our <a href="/contact" class="text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700 underline font-medium">Contact Page</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
